# Test phase and explicit caller contracts

This Source-only hold changes five runtime test files and removes their now
unused old void-entry imports in two files. It depends on the reviewed explicit
caller-clock proposal. No test, formatter, compiler, engine or scientific output
was executed or read, and canonical source is unchanged.

The shell and CTF02 initializer tests inspect allocation before BeginEnvrn.
Their temperature histories therefore assert zero allocation, while requested
zone-air temperatures remain 20, 17.25 and 23.5 on their separate actual owners.
The stale99 canary must not enter a fresh allocated surface history. Public
coefficient/time/count assertions are unchanged; no environment call is claimed.

`surface_ctf_history_terms_update_flux_constants` explicitly writes two authored
diagnostic coefficient/history rows. It now uses a detached cloned surface and
sets that local owner's public_num_ctf_terms to None. The original ordinary
State still owns Some(1); its public coefficient and lifecycle are unchanged.
All existing arithmetic and history-shift expectations are retained verbatim.

The five old manual void-entry calls migrate to the fallible explicit-clock
entry. One-step tests author Run/day1/hour/substep stamps from their actual
case arguments. Cached-vs-live schedule testing prepares the independent cached
State's caller explicitly, checks its retained Result boundary, and commits
only after success. All existing gain/radiant/temperature assertions remain.

The damping case already supplies 60 seconds. Its authored model now declares
60 steps/hour before generation; one real initial step enters the environment.
The test then assigns prior current surface40 and uses the next distinct step.
This prevents BeginEnvrn from overwriting the actual prior operand. The original
>25 damping assertion is unchanged. No clock is inferred from State counters.

The interzone numerical test is now explicitly diagnostic. Two authored
all-resistive rows use the existing coefficient-override initializer; no Native
result rows are read. Its supplied 60-second case has a matching authored
60-step/hour model. All original zone/surface/boundary numerical assertions
remain, with two direct existing surface_boundary_temperature_c checks added.
A separate real ordinary initializer regression requires UnsupportedBoundary;
the selected CON-01 boundary scope is not broadened or silently bypassed.

The existing missing-target regression remains unchanged. A separate production
boundary-reference preflight proposal restores that specific earlier validation
contract before public generation. This test package does not alter production
boundary calculations, ordinary generation, history implementation or any gate.

Root and an independent FULL Source peer must review these exact before/deltas
before application. Runtime failure evidence may expose further real physics
or scope issues; this hold does not predeclare success or change assertions to
fit observed results. Current liveordinary/Production tests and the new lifecycle
invalidation tests retain their real producer route.
